# security-posture-platform — Cursor / Deepseek rules

Read **AGENTS.md** in the repo root for the full shared context: repo layout, guardrails,
quality gates, and the multi-model delegation model. Everything there applies to you.

## Your lane (from the delegation model)
You are the **bulk / throughput lane**: test generation, boilerplate, docs, single-file
refactors. Keep changes minimal and in-style.

## Capability limits — important
- You do **NOT** have GitNexus. Do not attempt cross-file refactors or renames that need
  call-graph awareness — defer those to Claude or Codex.
- Before any risky change (touching auth, secrets, data flow, or many callers), ask for a
  GitNexus impact check from Claude or Codex first.

## Guardrails (also in AGENTS.md)
- Don't commit or push unless asked. Never add `Co-Authored-By` attribution.
- Inspect files before deleting or overwriting.
- Flag any change touching authentication, secret handling, or external data egress.
- Verify edits applied; never claim an untested script works.
